39, "direction": "in", "window": [51612, 58011]}, "result_digest": "ca22c21b8cd07769", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"in\", \"n_neighbors\": 3, \"neighbors\": [1344, 1539, 1544], \"node\": 1439, \"window\": [51612, 58011]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 37341, "tokens_after": 37341, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_15", "tool": "khop_subgraph", "args": {"node": 1357, "k": 2, "window": [51612, 53411]}, "result_digest": "6dfcb30ab3136f37", "result_summary": "{\"center\": 1357, \"edges\": [[79, 277], [277, 79], [277, 500], [277, 1057], [277, 1357], [500, 277], [1057, 277], [1357, 277]], \"k\": 2, \"n_edges\": 8, \"n_nodes\": 5, \"nodes\": [79, 277, 500, 1057, 1357], \"truncated\": false}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 45857, "tokens_after": 45857, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "khop_subgraph", "args": {"node": 1357, "k": 3, "window": [51612, 58011]}, "result_digest": "8145e6f6ba94bc29", "result_summary": "{\"center\": 1357, \"edges\": [[79, 277], [79, 512], [79, 1983], [191, 500], [277, 79], [277, 500], [277, 1057], [277, 1357], [333, 854], [333, 1357], [488, 500], [500, 191], [500, 277], [500, 488], [500, 770], [512, 79], [525, 785], [525, 1357], [770, 500], [785, 525], [786, 818], [818, 786], [818, 1259], [818, 1376], [854, 333], [1057, 277], [1057, 1335], [1057, 1787], [1057, 1876], [1259, 818], [1335, 1057], [1357, 277], [1357, 333], [1357, 525], [1357, 1376], [1357, 1595], [1376, 818], [1376, 1357], [1595, 1357], [1787, 1057], [1876, 1057], [1983, 79]], \"k\": 3, \"n_edges\": 42, \"n_nodes\": 22, \"nodes\": [79, 191, 277, 333, 488, 500, 512, 525, 770, 785, 786, 818, 854, 1057, 1259, 1335, 1357, 1376, 1595, 1787, 1876, 1983], \"truncated\": false}", "latency_ms": 2, "tokens_before": 54604, "tokens_after": 54604, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_3c29ca6f", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1357, 1439], "window": [36012, 74411], "confidence": 0.87, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "Node 1357 is active only late in the window (0 events before 50411, 31 in the final bucket) while 1439's activity is front-loaded and ceases after 60011, so the two are largely anti-ordered in time. There is no direct 1357->1439 edge and their out/in neighbourhoods are disjoint, ruling out a 2-hop relay. Within the only overlapping band (~51612-58011), 1357's out-set {277,333,525,1376,1595} and 1439's in-set {1344,1539,1544} are disjoint, and a full 3-hop expansion from 1357 in that band spans only 22 nodes, none of which is 1439 or feeds it. High total volume and high degree of both hubs are confounders that do not create any 600-unit-gap-respecting path. Conclusion: no genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**Temporal profiles are nearly disjoint and anti-ordered.** Node 1357 has *zero* events in [36012, 50411] and ramps up late (31 events in the final bucket), while 1439's activity is front-loaded (34 events in the first bucket) and drops to *zero* after 60011 (steps 07, 08). A cascade requires 1357 to act *before* 1439 receives influence, but 1357's activity mostly occurs after 1439 has gone silent.\n\n**No direct edge** exists in either direction (step 03), and 1357's 68 out-neighbors share no members with 1439's 67 in-neighbors (steps 04, 05) \u2014 so there is no 2-hop relay either.\n\n**The only temporal overlap is the thin band ~[51612, 58011]** (steps 09\u201312). Restricted to that band, 1357 reaches only {277, 333, 525, 1376, 1595} and 1439 is fed only by {1344, 1539, 1544} \u2014 disjoint sets (steps 13, 14). Expanding to **3 hops** from 1357 in that band yields just 22 nodes, containing neither 1439 nor any of its in-neighbors (steps 15, 16). So even *ignoring* the 600-unit gap rule and edge direction, no short path exists during the only time both were live.\n\n**Confounder controls:** the window is busy (5,931 events, 1,914 nodes, repeat ratio 0.017 \u2014 step 01) and both endpoints are high-degree hubs (~69 partners each \u2014 step 02). That volume and popularity is exactly the \"insufficient on its own\" evidence; the *ordering* is what fails.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_3c29ca6f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1357, 1439],\n  \"window\": [36012, 74411],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 1357 is active only late in the window (0 events before 50411, 31 in the final bucket) while 1439's activity is front-loaded and ceases after 60011, so the two are largely anti-ordered in time. There is no direct 1357->1439 edge and their out/in neighbourhoods are disjoint, ruling out a 2-hop relay. Within the only overlapping band (~51612-58011), 1357's out-set {277,333,525,1376,1595} and 1439's in-set {1344,1539,1544} are disjoint, and a full 3-hop expansion from 1357 in that band spans only 22 nodes, none of which is 1439 or feeds it. High total volume and high degree of both hubs are confounders that do not create any 600-unit-gap-respecting path. Conclusion: no genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 63874, "total_output_tokens": 7450, "total_tokens": 71324, "total_latency_ms": 105884, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}